  "stages": [
    {
      "id": "information-researcher-notes",
      "type": "Information",
      "label": {
        "en-US": "Template notes (delete before fielding)"
      },
      "title": {
        "en-US": "Template notes"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "researcher-notes",
          "type": "text",
          "content": {
            "en-US": "## Discussion prototype: family reunions\n\n_Delete this screen before collecting any data._\n\nBased on the existing Network Canvas CEGRM template. Review language, family boundaries and support domains with local collaborators. This version starts with mother/father wording; Architect also offers egg/sperm wording or participant choice. Neither setting describes an entire population.\n\nThe people named in **People in your life** are marked `non_kin`; everyone the pedigree adds is not. The beyond-family stages and the family health-communication roles are filtered on that attribute. The pedigree itself draws only the participant and the people connected to them through family relationships, so the non-kin never appear on it.\n\nConsent, recruitment, privacy and recording procedures are placeholders requiring local ethics approval. Conduct each interview privately even if recruitment happens at a reunion. Never display one participant's health history to the reunion or merge relatives' maps by default.\n\nThe closing condition display uses unknown inheritance and hides inferred risk. It presents reported family history, not genetic counselling or risk assessment. The optional gender question controls shapes; AFAB/AMAB/UAAB annotations are not implemented. Record participant observations and map limitations as qualitative findings.\n\nCEGRM: Kenen & Peters (2001), https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1016627426430. Methods and clinical interpretation should be reviewed with Lori Erby and Laura Koehly."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "information-intro",
      "type": "EgoForm",
      "label": {
        "en-US": "Welcome and consent"
      },
      "introductionPanel": {
        "title": {
          "en-US": "About this interview"
        },
        "text": {
          "en-US": "## Your family and the people who support you\n\nThis demonstration maps family relationships, what you know about a family health condition, and the people you turn to for information or support. Use nicknames if you prefer. You can leave questions unanswered, pause, or stop.\n\nFor an actual study, the researcher must first explain the approved consent and privacy procedures. This example consent question is a placeholder."
        }
      },
      "form": {
        "fields": [
          {
            "variable": "participant_consent",
            "prompt": {
              "en-US": "Do you consent to participate in this study?"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ego-form-background",
      "type": "EgoForm",
      "label": {
        "en-US": "About you"
      },
      "skipLogic": {
        "action": "SKIP",
        "filter": {
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "c0a8f2d1-4b6e-4a9c-8f3d-2e7b1a5c9d40",
              "type": "ego",
              "options": {
                "attribute": "participant_consent",
                "operator": "EXACTLY",
                "value": false
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "destination": {
          "type": "finish"
        }
      },
      "introductionPanel": {
        "title": {
          "en-US": "A little about you"
        },
        "text": {
          "en-US": "A few short questions before we start on the map."
        }
      },
      "form": {
        "fields": [
          {
            "variable": "ego_age",
            "prompt": {
              "en-US": "How old are you?"
            }
          },
          {
            "variable": "ego_education",
            "prompt": {
              "en-US": "What is the highest level of education you have completed?"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "family-pedigree",
      "type": "FamilyPedigree",
      "label": {
        "en-US": "Family pedigree"
      },
      "interviewScript": "Build the pedigree with the participant rather than handing them the device. Published CEGRM sessions are co-constructed, and recent studies pre-populate the pedigree before the session and review it with the participant instead of drawing it from scratch — do that if your study design allows, since it substantially reduces burden.\n\nLiving status and birth year are collected while each person is added. The two questions after the pedigree is finalised are asked by tapping people on the finished tree. Take them slowly. Illness, testing and bereavement will often prompt a story; let it run, and capture it using your approved study procedure.\n\nDiscussion prototype: mother/father framing is a starting point for collaborator review, not an assumption about all Black families or reunion participants. Ask local partners about preferred wording. Gender identity drives the configurable person shapes separately from sex recorded at birth. Standard AFAB/AMAB/UAAB annotations are not yet displayed.",
      "subject": {
        "entity": "node",
        "type": "person"
      },
      "prompt": {
        "en-US": "Let's map out your family. Who is in it?"
      },
      "nodeConfiguration": {
        "nameAttribute": "name",
        "nameField": {
          "prompt": {
            "en-US": "Name (optional)"
          },
          "hint": {
            "en-US": "A first name or nickname is fine. If you don’t know it, leave this blank and they will be shown by how they are related to you."
          }
        },
        "sexAssignedAtBirthAttribute": "sexAssignedAtBirth",
        "egoAttribute": "is_ego"
      },
      "edgeConfiguration": {
        "type": "family_relationship",
        "kindAttribute": "relationshipKind",
        "gestationalCarrierAttribute": "isGestationalCarrier",
        "currentPartnerAttribute": "isActive"
      },
      "framing": "gendered",
      "completeness": {
        "scope": "grandparents",
        "enforcement": "recommended",
        "relativesNotRecordedAttribute": "relativesNotRecorded",
        "itemText": {
          "parents": {
            "listItem": {
              "en-US": "{isYou, select, true {{missing, plural, one {Add your other biological parent} other {Add your biological parents}}} other {{missing, plural, one {Add another biological parent for “{name}”} other {Add biological parents for “{name}”}}}}"
            }
          },
          "siblings": {
            "listItem": {
              "en-US": "{isYou, select, true {Add your biological brothers and sisters, or say you have none} other {Add biological brothers and sisters for “{name}”, or say they have none}}"
            },
            "noneButton": {
              "en-US": "{isYou, select, true {I have no biological siblings} other {“{name}” has no biological siblings}}"
            },
            "question": {
              "en-US": "{isYou, select, true {Do you have any biological brothers or sisters, including half-brothers and half-sisters?} other {Does {name} have any biological brothers or sisters, including half-brothers and half-sisters?}}"
            }
          },
          "children": {
            "listItem": {
              "en-US": "{isYou, select, true {Add your biological children, or say you have none} other {Add biological children for “{name}”, or say they have none}}"
            },
            "noneButton": {
              "en-US": "{isYou, select, true {I have no biological children} other {“{name}” has no biological children}}"
            },
            "question": {
              "en-US": "{isYou, select, true {Do you have any biological children?} other {Does {name} have any biological children?}}"
            }
          },
          "details": {
            "listItem": {
              "en-US": "{isYou, select, true {Some details are missing about you} other {Some details are missing for “{name}”}}"
            }
          }
        },
        "recommendedNote": {
          "en-US": "You can also continue without these by pressing Next again."
        }
      },
      "form": {
        "fields": [
          {
            "variable": "gender_identity",
            "prompt": {
              "en-US": "How does this person describe their gender, if you know?"
            },
            "hint": {
              "en-US": "Optional. Do not guess. You may leave this blank."
            }
          },
          {
            "variable": "living_status",
            "prompt": {
              "en-US": "Is this person living or deceased?"
            }
          },
          {
            "variable": "birth_year",
            "prompt": {
              "en-US": "What year was this person born?"
            },
            "hint": {
              "en-US": "Leave this blank if you do not know."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "nominationPrompts": [
        {
          "id": "nom-condition",
          "text": {
            "en-US": "Who in your family has had **this condition**?"
          },
          "attribute": "has_condition"
        },
        {
          "id": "nom-testing",
          "text": {
            "en-US": "Who has had **genetic testing** for it?"
          },
          "attribute": "had_testing"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "information-beyond-family",
      "type": "Information",
      "label": {
        "en-US": "Beyond the family"
      },
      "title": {
        "en-US": "The people beyond your family"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "beyond-text",
          "type": "text",
          "content": {
            "en-US": "You have mapped the people who belong in your family story. The next few screens add everyone else who matters — friends, colleagues, neighbours, people from groups you belong to, and the people who look after your health.\n\nThey will sit alongside your family on the same map."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ng-non-kin",
      "type": "NameGeneratorQuickAdd",
      "label": {
        "en-US": "People in your life"
      },
      "interviewScript": "The same person can belong in several of these questions. Add them once, then pick them from the panel of people already named rather than typing the name again.\n\nThe published instrument treats this step as widening the map to the participant's whole social universe, so do not rush it — friends and co-members of groups are where the spiritual and emotional domains usually turn out to live.",
      "subject": {
        "entity": "node",
        "type": "person"
      },
      "quickAdd": "name",
      "panels": [
        {
          "id": "already-mentioned",
          "title": {
            "en-US": "People you added earlier"
          },
          "dataSource": "existing",
          "filter": {
            "join": "AND",
            "rules": [
              {
                "id": "c0a8f2d1-4b6e-4a9c-8f3d-2e7b1a5c9d46",
                "type": "node",
                "options": {
                  "type": "person",
                  "attribute": "is_ego",
                  "operator": "NOT",
                  "value": true
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "c0a8f2d1-4b6e-4a9c-8f3d-2e7b1a5c9d47",
                "type": "node",
                "options": {
                  "type": "person",
                  "attribute": "non_kin",
                  "operator": "EXACTLY",
                  "value": true
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "prompts": [
        {
          "id": "p-friends",
          "text": {
            "en-US": "Who are the **friends** who matter most to you?"
          },
          "additionalAttributes": [
            {
              "variable": "non_kin",
              "value": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p-work",
          "text": {
            "en-US": "Who are the people you know through **work or study**?"
          },
          "additionalAttributes": [
            {
              "variable": "non_kin",
              "value": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p-groups",
          "text": {
            "en-US": "Who do you know through **groups you belong to** — a faith community, a team, a club, or a community you are part of online?"
          },
          "additionalAttributes": [
            {
              "variable": "non_kin",
              "value": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p-care",
          "text": {
            "en-US": "Who is involved in looking after your **health**?"
          },
          "additionalAttributes": [
            {
              "variable": "non_kin",
              "value": true
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bin-tie-type",
      "type": "CategoricalBin",
      "label": {
        "en-US": "How you know each person"
